things that built very, very slowly.\"","year":1994,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Musical Offspring","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MmXDbXI6Sqk"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Debut Studio Album","body":"Released in 1994, this was Jeff Buckley's only studio album during his lifetime. It received significant critical acclaim, performing particularly well in Europe where it found more success than in the United States. However, Columbia Records did not perceive it as a major commercial hit or discern a clear stylistic direction for Buckley's future, leading to limited support. The album's moderate commercial success compelled Buckley to spend years touring continuously, playing in small venues to sustain himself. \"sólo ese album grey en 1994.\"","year":1994,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Recordando a Jeff Buckley","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYB4LJSFwEo"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"His Only Album; Died Accidentally 1997","body":"Jeff Buckley released *Grace* in 1994 — his one and only studio album. Three years later he accidentally drowned in the Mississippi River. The album is now considered a classic and a testament to what might have been. \"Three years later he'd be dead, accidentally drowning in the Mississippi River.\"","year":1994,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"1994","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4Jvy4q40tuo"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":107836524388438,"artist":"Jeff Buckley","artist_id":125241476372574,"title":"Grace","year":1994,"ess":0,"yt":"5gcKMbr8SEI","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores lo-fi de los noventa","scene_id":4419681145361,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.6"],"pages":[[1,247,null]]}],"others":[{"id":86991094857534,